to Oregon, sources say","description":"Former Minnesota safety Koi Perich has committed to Oregon, sources told ESPN on Monday, confirming a report by CBS Sports.","published":"2026-01-13T03:22:44.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/47594926/minnesota-transfer-safety-koi-perich-commits-oregon-ducks-football","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas, Penn St. players lead AP preseason All-America 1st team","description":"Texas edge rusher Colin Simmons is among three Longhorns on The Associated Press All-America team. No. 2 Penn State also had three players, giving the Nittany Lions and Longhorns the most on the team.","published":"2025-08-18T20:05:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/46008870/texas-penn-st-players-lead-ap-preseason-all-america-1st-team","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bottom 10 after Week 12: How the Bruins put the 'L' in UCLA","description":"While UCLA suffered its first loss, we still have a team looking for its first win -- and time is running out.","published":"2026-11-25T12:14:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585901/bottom-10-week-12-ucla","type":"Story","byline":"Ryan McGee","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What went wrong for Michigan and Ohio State in 2026?","description":"Michigan and Ohio State have combined for nine losses entering Saturday's game.","published":"2026-11-25T12:25:19.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576202/michigan-wolverines-ohio-state-buckeyes-went-wrong","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg and Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Best bets for rivalry week: Breaking down Michigan-OSU, Iowa-Nebraska and more","description":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno break down the best bets they see around college football for rivalry week.","published":"2026-11-25T11:46:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50583508/college-football-betting-week-13-rivalry-week","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado and Mark Zinno","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-25T03:40:06.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"College football betting: Should you still bet on Indiana to make the CFP?","description":"The Hoosiers dropped to No. 14 in the latest CPF rankings, but are they still a good bet to make the playoff?","published":"2026-11-25T04:16:33.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50588403/2026-college-football-playoff-cfp-indiana-hoosiers","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 Anger Index: Indiana dropped how many spots?!","description":"Ranking the teams that should be most upset with the latest CFP rankings.","published":"2026-11-25T13:05:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50582371/cfp-ranking-2026-anger-index-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"David Hale","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the College Football Playoff bubble after committee's fourth ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-25T13:04:11.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575185/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-fourth-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Why UTEP-NIU is 2026's most unglamorous Game of the Century","description":"The Week 13 game will mark the first time since at least 2000 that two teams that are winless against FBS opponents will meet in their final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-25T01:19:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50587546/utep-niu-college-football-game-century","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5142588/koi-perich","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koi_Perich"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Koi Perich","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Koi_Perich","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-22T04:17:20Z","intro":"Koi Perich (born September 26, 2005) is an American college football safety for the Oregon Ducks. He previously played for the Minnesota Golden Gophers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Perich attended Esko High School in Esko, Minnesota. As a junior, he rushed for over 800 yards, notched 75 tackles, two sacks, three interceptions, four forced fumbles, and 25 touchdowns. In the first game of his senior season, Perich intercepted two passes which he returned both for touchdowns. As a senior, he amassed 27 total touchdowns: 16 rushing, five defensive, four return, one passing, and one receiving. Perich also notched 76 tackles, three interceptions, and four fumble recoveries on defense, earning all-state recognition. He accepted an invite to play in the All-American Bowl, where he intercepted a pass on the goal line and blocked a punt en route to earning game MVP honors.\n\nRECRUITING\nPerich received offers from schools such as USC, Michigan, Wisconsin, Minnesota, Iowa and Washington, as well as late offers from Florida State and Ohio State. He committed to play college football for the Minnesota Golden Gophers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a freshman, Perich recorded 24 solo tackles, one pass defended, one forced fumble, and five interceptions. He was named first-team All-Big Ten Conference and second-team All-American following the conclusion of the regular season.\nKoi Perich entered his sophomore season in 2025 with increased responsibilities across defense, special teams, and occasional offensive snaps. Mistakes early in the season led to a reduction of offensive snaps, but Perich scored a game winning touchdown on his first career defensive score to win the schools 2025 homecoming game against Purdue.\nOn January 1, 2026, Perich announced that he would enter the transfer portal.\nOn January 12, 2026, Perich announced that he would be transferring to the University of Oregon."}]}}